{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Information Design"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about information design. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Identify and recognize information related to concepts about graphic design related to IT."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.   Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about \u201cinformation design\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down the most important aspects about graphics and variables for information design. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think about your favorite topic (sports, music, fashion etc.) and make a summary about it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a graphic in a poster explaining the topic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your graphic or chart with your class and explain it"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about the concept of information design."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I summarize important information related to information design."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a graphic to present my favorite topic in class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share and explain the graphic in class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use adjectives to compare nouns and say which one has a more developed quality than the other."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To use <b>comparatives</b>, you need to consider the length of the adjective you are going to use. Remember, you make comparisons between two nouns which share one quality, but one has a more developed level of that quality."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b><i>Short Adjectives</b></i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you have short adjectives (which have one or two syllables), you add er at the end to make the comparative form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><i> Diagrams are <b>easier</b> to read <b>than</b> long texts.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Information design is concerned with making information easier to grasp."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Reorganize the information to make it clearer and more appealing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><b>Long Adjectives </b></i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For long adjectives (which have more than two syllables), you need to use the word more before the adjective. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><i> Maps are <b>more helpful than</b> spoken directions.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In both cases, you use than to introduce the second noun in the comparison."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present of Verb to Be With Verbs in Past Participle"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the verb to be in present to describe people or things. <i>Past participles</i> can be used as adjectives. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you are describing one object, you use the form is. If you are talking about many objects, you use the form are. In addition, to create past participles, you can add ed to regular verbs, but irregular verbs have different changes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the following structure: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center>Subject + be (<b>am/is/are</b>) + verb in past participle form (-ed) + complement</center>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm trying to figure out this information, but it is complicated."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's the way statistics are presented, so that people can get the information quickly and efficiently."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:</br><i> Information design <b>is developed</b> to improve presentations. </br>Diagrams <b>are organized</b> to present concise information.</i>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "figure out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to understand or comprehend something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm trying to figure out this information, but it is complicated."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "diagram"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a figure or chart that summarizes some information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What do you think I should do with this diagram?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "appealing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "attractive or nice-looking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Reorganize the information to make it clearer and more appealing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "arrange"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to organize: to put i