], "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Let's present some information with clear variables about the most important topic for me"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n4le02ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> I can't believe this. I'm trying to figure out this information, but it is complicated.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Jack:</span> Wow, it looks like a very ineffective diagram. The information design is quite bad.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> I know. Information design is concerned with making information easier to grasp.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Jack:</span> Indeed. Did you know that maps and other diagrams are designed to help people understand large amounts of information?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Really? Do you know how they appeared?<br />"}, {"time": "25300", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jack:</span>  Well, they appeared around the 19th century. The first diagrams were maps that helped people understand something, like variables that are related. For example, a map that shows how a country's borders have changed over time. In this case, we have the variables of time and size.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span>  That's very interesting. What do you think I should do with this diagram?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Jack:</span>  Well, you can try to make it more effective than it is. Reorganize the information to make it clearer and more appealing. In fact, what do you need it for?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span>  I need to prepare a presentation. <br />"}, {"time": "57000", "image": "enpe8n4le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jack:</span> I see. In that case, you can make it simpler than it is already. Since you want to present the information, select and arrange it hierarchically making sure it is developed in a way that attracts people's attention, and finally, make sure you're using the right materials, size, etc. That's the way statistics are presented, so that people can get the information quickly and efficiently. And it is something that we have been doing for a long time, for example in traffic signs, labels, product manuals and banners.<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Wow, I didn't know that information design is so generalized nowadays. Anyway, I will rearrange the information in a more effective diagram so that viewers can understand this complex information in a breeze."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n4le02ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}